 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The plan's title «الإصلاح ما استطعت» was the verse itself (88:25-27): now «غاية المصلح». Their mockery (87) is framed («على وجه التهكم», «من احتيال ومكر», «استهزاءً به»). Coins for «أموالنا». 88 is Shu'ayb's speech: only geometric on «وما توفيقي إلا بالله عليه توكلت وإليه أنيب». No plate on the prophets' names in 89. STAGING v4: Same market street as 11_84-86: Shu'ayb a blue drop labelled Shu'ayb (no plate on his name, no close-up or pan on his drop), his people three faceless men in dark robes. c1 (87): they speak to Shu'ayb (87:1) in mockery (framed by the glosses); the camera on them (87:3, 87:11); nobody turns toward an empty side while their fathers' worship is named (87:6-9: no idol and no place for one); a coins plate for our wealth (87:14-15); they point at Shu'ayb on 87:17 (you are the forbearing, said in mockery, Al-Muyassar: mocking him). c2 (88): Shu'ayb answers (88:1, 88:22); a seal plate for clear proof from my Lord (88:7-9), a wheat plate for a good provision (88:12-13); the camera on them for I do not want to do what I forbid you (88:17; nothing acted inside the negation); geometric for my success is only through Allah, on Him I rely (88:28-35); no glow, no raised hands. c3 (89): Shu'ayb warns them (89:1, 89:18), the camera on them for the warning (89:3); no plate over the names of Nuh, Hud, Salih and Lut (89:10-20), the camera is wide there; an hourglass for not far from you (89:21-22, Al-Muyassar: neither in place nor in time). Cover: Shu'ayb speaking for I only want reform."
